  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The mechanism of basic amide hydrolysis begins with the nucleophilic addition of a hydroxide ion at the carbonyl carbon creating a tetrahedral alkoxide intermediate. In the given case ring opening reaction takes place. On acidification, we get a secondary aino acid.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0044_deab9c18f664.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 279px;\" /></p>"
